1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:04,140
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,201
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,740
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,917
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,420
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,677
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:16,820
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,197
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,297
We came to this new world believing.

11
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,957
That surely someday we
just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,297
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,997
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,200
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,637
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,177
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,877
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,860
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up, way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if brains
are up, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,677
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,160
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:33,700
That creature, it's a slime, isn't it?

54
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:35,290
A what?

55
00:02:35,373 --> 00:02:39,637
I thought that slimes were limited to
the realm of fantasy, but apparently not.

56
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:43,367
I read a book about a slime, and
it looked just like that one.

57
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,421
There's nothing else it could be.

58
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,264
The book was quite fascinating.

59
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:49,893
I couldn't put it down.

60
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:53,100
This slime you see loved
to attack beautiful women.

61
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:57,535
Its body fluids were harmless, but
they had a knack for melting clothes.

62
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,720
Oh, naughty.

63
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,160
That monster is pretty messed up, huh?

64
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:08,240
Uh, by the way, can I borrow that book?

65
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,517
Could I borrow it, too?

66
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:10,659
Would you shut up?

67
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:11,720
Just look.

68
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:17,737
If that thing touches you, it's going to
do a lot worse than just melt your clothes.

69
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:22,349
The fish are dying from the little pieces
of itself that dropped in the lake.

70
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,588
The thing's made of poison.

71
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:29,466
It only takes a drop to kill,
and it looks like it's spreading.

72
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:30,560
It's poison?

73
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:33,860
Wait, but the samurai's
torso is in that lake.

74
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,237
Surely not you're diving in, sanji.

75
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:51,880
I brought him with us, so
I can't let him die here.

76
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:56,737
I may be a woman right now,
but it's time to man up.

77
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:59,297
I'm proud of you.

78
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,397
Handle the ones behind you!

79
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:04,540
I won't be too long. Huh? Behind me?

80
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:09,100
A veritable puffy of many slimes!

81
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,791
What'd you think in here?

82
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,380
Nami, I'm sorry.

83
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:15,522
But still, I'm the strongest
swimmer on the crew.

84
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:19,581
I swear I'll be done before anything
happens to your gorgeous body!

85
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:21,650
Careful!

86
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:23,115
Good luck down there!

87
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,700
This is even colder than it looks!

88
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,900
I better make this quick!

89
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,200
Monet's alone.

90
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,480
This is my chance.

91
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:46,480
Sorry, the Master's not here. Yeah?

92
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:47,780
Where'd he go?

93
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,318
Probably outside to watch the fight.

94
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:53,655
That degenerate can't get
enough death and destruction.

95
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,640
That's all right.

96
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,797
I don't need him.

97
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,762
I think I'll be taking off soon.

98
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,515
I've seen everything.

99
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,367
I'm through with this place.

100
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,390
Shame.

101
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,260
It'll be lonely without you.

102
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:10,820
I could use your help with
something first, though.

103
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,626
Could I borrow you for a sec?

104
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,700
What is this? A date?

105
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,260
Lucky me.

106
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:22,880
A man of few words, are we? Where to?

107
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:24,100
You'll see.

108
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:25,530
All right.

109
00:05:25,613 --> 00:05:27,040
I was bored anyway.

110
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:34,340
That must be the bird Lady
Usopp was talking about.

111
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:42,460
Straw Hat caught the master!

112
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,480
Way to go, Luffy!

113
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,840
Little punk, how dare you!

114
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,020
Crazy kid.

115
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,340
Let go, you fool!

116
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,060
So that's Haki.

117
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,524
Caesar has Logia powers, right?

118
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:58,677
But Luffy can still grab him
even though he's made of gas.

119
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:59,837
Back off, Straw Hat!

120
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:00,880
We'll soothe!

121
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:02,450
Hurry!

122
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:03,757
Take him out, quick!

123
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:07,193
If you jerks want to pick a
fight, then pick one with me!

124
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:08,560
And clutch!

125
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,820
Out of my way!

126
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,580
Luffy's got this one.

127
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:16,408
Caesar can't use his power.

128
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,520
Not exactly.

129
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,015
I wouldn't celebrate.

130
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:23,860
With Armament Haki, Luffy
is able to touch Caesar,

131
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:26,020
even though he has Logia powers.

132
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,445
However, unlike ocean
water or sea prism stone,

133
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,877
it doesn't actually weaken
the person that he touches.

134
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:37,372
We don't know the full extent
of the Gas-Gasfruit's power.

135
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,308
This is only the beginning.

136
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:45,800
Don't get cocky, you brat!

137
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:48,197
Armament hardening!

138
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,110
Nick!

139
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,280
Gum-Gum!

140
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,880
Gas robe!

141
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,840
What's going on here?

142
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,520
I can't get away!

143
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:02,990
Oop!

144
00:07:03,073 --> 00:07:05,940
Just suck it up and
die already, would you?

145
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,900
I promise it'll be fun!

146
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,340
For me!

147
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,320
Luffy! Dammit!

148
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:15,817
I've performed countless experiments.

149
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:18,217
And I can assure you that
my gas will subject you?

150
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,653
to only the most exquisite of suffering.

151
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,740
I think he's lost his mind.

152
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,320
No, Joe, he's done for.

153
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:32,009
He's sucking up all of it.

154
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,060
He's screwed now.

155
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,700
I'm afraid to watch it.

156
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,130
Neat.

157
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:53,237
I guess poison doesn't
bother me too much anymore.

158
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,026
Probably because of Magellan.

159
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:58,890
Magellan?

160
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,720
The prison guard with
the parimethia powers?

161
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:04,820
My poison's potency makes his look puny!

162
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,540
Now, gong gong!

163
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,400
Get me!

164
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:17,770
Master!

165
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,580
How dare you!

166
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:22,269
We won't let you lay
another finger on him!

167
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:27,820
Mind your own business,
you maggots! Master?

168
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:39,060
He didn't just call us maggots, did he?

169
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,240
We must have heard him wrong. Gum-Gum!

170
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:44,130
Let's go!

171
00:08:44,213 --> 00:08:46,160
Gunfire! Gah!

172
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,300
And Dasta Net!

173
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:08,850
Huffy!

174
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,417
All right, Master!

175
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:17,260
I think we've had enough fun for
today, wake up my smileys, wake up!

176
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:19,020
Smileys? Huh?

177
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,140
They're moving, how do they do that?

178
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:32,820
Very good, now give Straw
Hat a big hug, go! No!

179
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:39,557
They can follow orders?

180
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:41,405
I thought they were just goop.

181
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,600
Luffy, run away!

182
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,500
Those slime guys blow up!

183
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:52,100
Um, woo-wee! Luffy!

184
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,871
It's time to say goodbye!

185
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,210
Gastonet!

186
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:09,950
Luffy!

187
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,530
He he he!

188
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:34,990
What?

189
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:40,980
All right.

190
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:46,680
Com-com-jecture!

191
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,700
No! Master!

192
00:10:57,280 --> 00:11:00,620
Those slimy dudes blow up like crazy.

193
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,460
Look at that!

194
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,875
Getting us all worked up over nothing!

195
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,727
Muffy's got this in the bag!

196
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:07,800
I hope so.

197
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,580
Damn, that kid's tough!

198
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:11,260
Just let him handle this.

199
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,080
Round two!

200
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,920
You gotta fight us too!

201
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:17,865
If that's what you want, sure!

202
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:26,760
Okay, I got you for
real this time! Master!

203
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,030
Robin!

204
00:11:29,113 --> 00:11:29,943
Franky!

205
00:11:30,026 --> 00:11:31,697
Is there anything here I can put him in?

206
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:34,297
He's got Logia power,
so we can't tie him up.

207
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:36,204
So, like a barrel or something?

208
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:37,450
Whoa, whoa!

209
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,520
Not so fast!

210
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:41,577
The Navy is taking him
into custody, so step back!

211
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:44,557
You might as well turn
yourself in while you're at it!

212
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,400
Hands up, pirate scum!

213
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:47,920
So what now?

214
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:50,160
Do we fight the Straw Hats or not?

215
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:55,830
Straw Hat!

216
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:01,960
What's wrong?

217
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:20,100
You shouldn't underestimate me.

218
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:55,680
Oh, my God.

219
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,160
Show yourself.

220
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,520
Who are you?

221
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:07,640
It's me.

222
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:15,597
Why aren't you here?

223
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:17,060
Why now?

224
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:26,480
How many years has it been?

225
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,120
Look at you, all grown up.

226
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:31,950
Long.

227
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:49,017
You think the boss doesn't
know what's going on?

228
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:51,394
I had hoped you were smarter than that.

229
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:58,601
To be honest with you, we don't
trust this Caesar character either.

230
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:01,957
The guy is shady.

231
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:05,197
That's why the boss sent an
undercover agent to the island.

232
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:07,480
The lovely monet here.

233
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,517
Rumor has it, you're a warlord now.

234
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,640
That's one hell of a promotion.

235
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,040
When did you get here?

236
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:21,550
Fair go.

237
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,517
Actually, I just arrived.

238
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:28,277
I was spending some time in Dressrosa.

239
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,640
I hitched a ride on a S .A .D.

240
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:34,880
tanker leaving port And now, it
seems that was the right move

241
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,020
What do you mean by that?

242
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,900
Why target me?

243
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:42,120
I didn't do a damn thing to you No,

244
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:45,020
not yet anyway Because if you had,

245
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,797
you'd be dead right now I
hate to break it to you,

246
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:50,320
but there's no fooling us grown-ups. Law.

247
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:56,920
Well, in that case, I
should just finish you!

248
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:58,680
Oh, yeah.

249
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:01,080
One more thing before I go.

250
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,940
Show some respect, kid.

251
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:13,240
It's Mr.

252
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:14,380
Vergo to you.

253
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:37,180
What the heck happened here?

254
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:39,140
I got no idea.

255
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:41,724
What do you think we should do?

256
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:45,740
He's got Tashigi.

257
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:48,046
Now, that's Smoker, remember?

258
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:58,017
You know, I never thought I'd see the Vice
Admiral get knocked out twice in one day.

259
00:15:58,100 --> 00:16:00,453
And he's not the only one who went down.

260
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:02,462
Three of the Straw Hats did too.

261
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:04,897
Think the Master used conquerors, Haki?

262
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,156
Don't be ridiculous.

263
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,777
There's no way he could be
that much stronger than them.

264
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,797
Then what was it?

265
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:13,097
I mean, he beat all of them without
even laying a finger on him.

266
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,239
Well, that was fun while it lasted.

267
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:23,617
that's what you get maybe you should
have known better than to mess with the

268
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:26,897
master he is our god of salvation master

269
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:30,457
master master master

270
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:35,637
master master now we

271
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:40,357
mustn't waste any time my strong soldiers
hurry and tie these five pirate scoundrels

272
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:45,637
up at once you see prism stone shackles
on the power holders once you're done i

273
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:49,797
want you to move out leave the sailors
behind and seek refuge inside the lab it's

274
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:50,837
far too dangerous out

275
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:56,977
here i'm sure you've

276
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:58,617
all noticed the strange substance that's

277
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:02,417
been raining down from the sky there's
no cause for concern i will ensure your

278
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:08,660
safety okay thank you master it seems the
yeti cool brothers failed at their task

279
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:12,300
Oh, well, I can't blame them.

280
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:17,841
I guess the combination of Straw Hat and
Law was simply too much for them to handle.

281
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:29,830
Ah!

282
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,059
Right in the face!

283
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:34,010
No!

284
00:17:34,093 --> 00:17:35,020
It's poison gas!

285
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:36,160
My eyes!

286
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,160
My eyes!

287
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:39,490
Oh, wait.

288
00:17:39,573 --> 00:17:41,600
I don't have any eyes. Guess what?

289
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,289
I'm immune to your attack.

290
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:45,598
Now fight me to let in this villain.

291
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:48,620
I'm not again.

292
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:51,457
Seems we can't use our
swords against them.

293
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:52,800
They spit poison gas.

294
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:55,157
Why'd you go and poke the damn thing?

295
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,677
You saw what it did to me.

296
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:59,407
I thought that maybe it
just didn't like you.

297
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:02,587
What are we going to do now?

298
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:04,191
We've got nowhere to run.

299
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,150
Hey, I know.

300
00:18:05,233 --> 00:18:06,337
They're made of jelly, right?

301
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:07,977
I think you should try eating one.

302
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,340
What? No way!

303
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:12,817
I wish you'd stop bullying me
into things like this, Zoro!

304
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:15,160
I'm nearly 70 years older than you!

305
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,120
Fine, sorry I asked.

306
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,438
Never mind Grandpa.

307
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:20,357
I know you didn't just call me that!

308
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:22,675
I'm no Grandpa, I'm a lively skeleton!

309
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,320
Whoa, what's wrong with him?

310
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:29,317
Damn, it's cold.

311
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,820
Sorry about this, Nami.

312
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:33,650
What's that?

313
00:18:33,733 --> 00:18:35,836
Is it the slime's venom or something?

314
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:38,217
Oh, that's just great!

315
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:42,697
Here's hoping the torso is not stuck
in the middle of that poisonous cloud.

316
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:46,737
I've been using observation Haki for a
while now and I haven't found anything.

317
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:48,437
It must be getting weak;

318
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:51,197
I can't tell the difference
between its life force

319
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:54,740
and the fish that are
swimming around a shark.

320
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:01,800
Are you kidding me?

321
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:14,260
Are you feeling all right, Mr. Samurai?

322
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:15,717
Hey, what's the matter?

323
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,506
You look like you're in pain.

324
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,300
Oh, no, you don't!

325
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:23,342
You're not getting away from me!

326
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:34,520
Stop chewing on it, you bastard!

327
00:19:35,620 --> 00:19:38,440
This doesn't hurt, it merely itches a bit!

328
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:41,260
Jeez, what's gotten into this guy?

329
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,993
It must be dreadful to sound like those.

330
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:47,160
I'm fine!

331
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:49,740
Maybe something happened to Sanji?

332
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,280
Let go of it or else, shark!

333
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:17,217
I've got the last piece
of the samurai puzzle now,

334
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,437
we can put the poor bastard
back together again.

335
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:22,097
I gotta hurry and get the shore.

336
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:25,260
Oh, it's closing up!

337
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:43,920
The poison already got this far?

338
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,340
Now what'll I do?

339
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,089
I'm completely surrounded.

340
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:51,777
Is Nami's body strong enough
to get me out of this?

341
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:54,272
I guess there's only one way to find out.

342
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:57,042
It's not looking good for Sanji.

343
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:59,337
The whole lake is turning
the color of the poison.

344
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,420
He'd better hurry and come ashore.

345
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:07,510
Walk!

346
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,976
Don't close up!

347
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:17,290
Walk!

348
00:21:17,373 --> 00:21:19,000
He made it out alive! Sure did.

349
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,940
And he's got the torso.

350
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,300
Just like you said he would!

351
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:30,100
What can I say here?

352
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:33,977
I feared I would never have
my body back as it should be.

353
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:37,100
But thanks to you, I'm a
whole samurai once again.

354
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:49,777
Whoa, I must admit, you're a lot
taller than I expected you to be.

355
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:51,684
Even taller than me, I believe.

356
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,294
Why, yes, that's true.

357
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:55,366
Allow me to introduce myself.

358
00:21:56,740 --> 00:21:58,880
Gentlemen, I am the samurai Kidamon.

359
00:21:59,580 --> 00:22:03,657
I hailed from a town called Kuri, in
the land of Wano, if you're not aware.

360
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:05,505
Can somebody help me out here?

361
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:07,826
I'm about to freeze to death.

362
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:09,920
Yes, sorry to keep you waiting.

363
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,699
This should do it.

364
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:16,900
It's still cold.

365
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:20,057
That coat's going to disappear
once he takes it off, right?

366
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:22,217
What shall I call you, curly eyebrow?

367
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:25,476
I would like to know your
honorable name, my good sir.

368
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,277
Fine, my name is Sanji.

369
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:30,100
Cut the sir crap, okay?

370
00:22:30,540 --> 00:22:33,637
What, you get your body back and all
of a sudden you start acting like Mr.

371
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:34,550
Manners?

372
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:36,937
I put my neck out to help you
when you were just a severed head.

373
00:22:37,020 --> 00:22:40,437
But instead of being appreciative,
you kept hurling insults at me.

374
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:42,285
Do you remember what you said?

375
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,420
If only I had known sooner.

376
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,500
I loathe pirates.

377
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:52,557
Though I should have guessed.

378
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,581
That does explain your barbarism.

379
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:58,240
You're on my last nerve.

380
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:01,660
All you have to say is
help me find my body.

381
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:06,320
Asking for help from you,
pirates, I would rather die!

382
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:07,990
Yes,

383
00:23:08,073 --> 00:23:09,997
but I'm sure you must pity
a poor disembodied head

384
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:12,557
who can't even defend
himself if someone attacks.

385
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:14,405
So would you like to carry me?

386
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,240
I'm a horrible person.

387
00:23:25,620 --> 00:23:27,000
Please forgive me.

388
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:29,560
I owe you my life.

389
00:23:29,940 --> 00:23:31,822
I'll never forget your kindness.

390
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:33,940
Not as long as I live.

391
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:37,297
I insulted you and your
friends, yet you rescued me.

392
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:40,077
I doubted you when you swore
to make me whole again.

393
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,572
And I wasn't convinced until it happened.

394
00:23:43,140 --> 00:23:44,040
Forgive me.

395
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:45,540
I'm backing you.

396
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:47,525
I don't deserve your kindness.

397
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:49,497
I never should have doubted you.

398
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:51,097
What the hell are you doing?

399
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:52,709
Lift your head, you idiot.

400
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:55,077
No man should ever get
down on his knees and beg.

401
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,477
You got that? Yeah.

402
00:23:56,560 --> 00:24:01,540
I was just thinking,
without you, I would be...

403
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,230
Sorry.

404
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:07,129
As much as I hate to interrupt
this touching moment, I must.

405
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:11,506
You see, it would appear that
we're in mortal danger right now.

406
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:15,860
Thanks to our colorful friend.

407
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,477
What's with all the slime guys?

408
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:29,266
I thought I told you to
do something about it.

409
00:24:29,740 --> 00:24:34,317
Well we tried and didn't work, so we
just gave up—what were we supposed to do?

410
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:36,477
You chump, shouldn't
have given up so easily?

411
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:38,417
We've got to stop it somehow.

412
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:41,977
We all know that Nami would kill me if
anything were to happen to this body.

413
00:24:42,060 --> 00:24:48,437
You are never gonna

414
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:49,377
give it back to her.

415
00:24:49,460 --> 00:24:50,290
Are you, nope?

416
00:24:50,373 --> 00:24:51,497
No way in hell!

417
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:55,357
If I may make a suggestion—why don't
we try to destroy it with fire?

418
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:59,197
Huh, see my blade—it burns as it cuts.

419
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:01,677
That's why I am known as Fox Fire. Keen?

420
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:05,957
Em on allow me to blaze a
path so that we may escape.

421
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:09,157
You can burn and...

422
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:10,828
can burn and Slice enemies?

423
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:13,360
Sounds a lot like magic if you ask me.

424
00:26:01,460 --> 00:26:03,660
You cut through it? No way.

425
00:26:04,580 --> 00:26:06,639
I've cleared our path of the slime.

426
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:08,457
I'm coming for you, Momonosuke!

427
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:10,900
How are we still alive?

428
00:26:11,360 --> 00:26:14,137
I thought we were engulfed by the
fire from that massive explosion,

429
00:26:14,220 --> 00:26:15,573
but I suppose not, huh?

430
00:26:15,940 --> 00:26:17,020
Excuse me, Mr.

431
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:20,757
Kin'emon, if you wouldn't mind,
could you explain what just happened?

432
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:22,220
I don't mind at all.

433
00:26:22,460 --> 00:26:24,107
I cut through the explosion.

434
00:26:24,460 --> 00:26:25,657
And how'd you do that?

435
00:26:25,740 --> 00:26:27,800
My foxfire-style slices with flame.

436
00:26:27,980 --> 00:26:31,117
And through the knowledge and
use of my myriad of secret arts,

437
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:33,494
I am able to cut through flame as well.

438
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:36,680
There is no fire that can
withstand my blade. None.

439
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:42,120
Now then, Momonosuke is in danger.

440
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:44,097
I must go and rescue him.

441
00:26:44,180 --> 00:26:45,560
I'll take my leave.

442
00:26:54,900 --> 00:26:55,797
Hang on!

443
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:58,537
I've always wanted to
see a samurai in action.

444
00:26:58,620 --> 00:27:01,680
Tell you what, Kin'emon,
I'll help you save your son.

445
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:07,510
You
